From 4f1012500c512d57fb7e9059099bbb7a96f3e311 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fast_sync(v2): adapt 256-shard UTXO SnapSync and reverse peel
 to V2 header state_root

Bind 256-shard UTXO SnapSync and bijective reverse block peeling directly
to the 134-byte V2 block header state_root.

Original-Commit: 2d9971f6c7de3fb3ffd09ff8a9964a65537dde8a
Original-Patch: v2/019
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Application pass preserves the original native V2 sync/header adapter and original native fault-injection fixture, rather than redesigning it. Shared022/023 eCash adapter remains in its earlier prefix; native methods introduced107 replace that adapter only after native consensus. Retain current processor/serving setup and timeout/body-callback interfaces. UNRESOLVED correctness comparison required for anchor authentication, atomic pivot import, restart provenance, full reverse validation and requested-body/deadline behavior; no equivalence or safety parity is claimed.
